RoutyRnS 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="144"/> <img width="327" height="144" src="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-11/Students%20of%20the%20Laborie%20BOy%27s%20Primary%20School%20with%20the%20Tsunami%20Ready%20Project%20Local%20Facilitator%20and%20Teacher_0.jpg.webp?itok=RoutyRnS" alt="" loading="lazy" class="img-fluid" /> </picture><span class="submenu-text">Taking action</span></div></a></div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></li><li class="menu-item nav-item"> <span class="nav-link dropdown-toggle" data-bs-toggle="dropdown-menu" title="Expand menu Governance">Governance</span><div class="big menu_link_content menu-link-contentmain view-mode-level-0 dropdown-menu bg-primary menu-dropdown-0 menu-type-level_0"><div class="row submenu-wrapper"><div class="left-wrapper col-lg-3 col-md-12"><div class="field field--name-field-description field--type-string-long field--label-hidden field__item">International cooperation and coordination lie at the heart of our collective safety.</div><div class="field field--name-field-links field--type-link field--label-hidden menu-links field__items"><div class="field__item menu-link"><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/en/coordination-and-information">ICGs &amp; TICs</a></div><div class="field__item menu-link"><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/en/working-groups">Working Groups</a></div></div></div><div class="right-wrapper col-lg-9 col-md-12"><div class="main-navigation collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="menu nav navbar-nav menu-level-1"><li class="menu-item nav-item"> <a href="/en/pacific" class="nav-link" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/48">Pacific Ocean</a><div class="menu_link_content menu-link-contentmain view-mode-level-1 level-1-submenu"> <a href="/en/pacific" class="submenu"><div class="submenu-big card card-overlay"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_desktop/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=4OFWTZ5g 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="200" height="264"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_tablet/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=4UqDRZp6 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="163" height="216"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=_kSbCecb 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="144"/> <img width="327" height="144" src="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=_kSbCecb" alt="" loading="lazy" class="img-fluid" /> </picture><span class="submenu-text">Pacific Ocean</span></div></a></div></li><li class="menu-item nav-item"> <a href="/en/indian-ocean" class="nav-link" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/49">Indian Ocean</a><div class="menu_link_content menu-link-contentmain view-mode-level-1 level-1-submenu"> <a href="/en/indian-ocean" class="submenu"><div class="submenu-big card card-overlay"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_desktop/public/2024-02/Indian%20Ocean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=Xsmjh4Gv 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="200" height="264"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_tablet/public/2024-02/Indian%20Ocean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=TBQWiLEA 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="163" height="216"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Indian%20Ocean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=r-31Bmky 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="144"/> <img width="327" height="144" src="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Indian%20Ocean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=r-31Bmky" alt="" loading="lazy" class="img-fluid" /> </picture><span class="submenu-text">Indian Ocean</span></div></a></div></li><li class="menu-item nav-item"> <a href="/en/neam" class="nav-link" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/50">North-Eastern Atlantic &amp; Mediterranean</a><div class="menu_link_content menu-link-contentmain view-mode-level-1 level-1-submenu"> <a href="/en/neam" class="submenu"><div class="submenu-big card card-overlay"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_desktop/public/2024-02/Mediterranean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=KORlJtB_ 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="200" height="264"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_tablet/public/2024-02/Mediterranean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=TP0r_zyG 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="163" height="216"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Mediterranean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=eG_ETFwt 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="144"/> <img width="327" height="144" src="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Mediterranean%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=eG_ETFwt" alt="" loading="lazy" class="img-fluid" /> </picture><span class="submenu-text">North-Eastern Atlantic &amp; Mediterranean</span></div></a></div></li><li class="menu-item nav-item"> <a href="/en/caribbean" class="nav-link" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/51">Caribbean</a><div class="menu_link_content menu-link-contentmain view-mode-level-1 level-1-submenu"> <a href="/en/caribbean" class="submenu"><div class="submenu-big card card-overlay"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_desktop/public/2024-02/Caribbean%20sunset%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=O7GHdCHi 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="200" height="264"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_tablet/public/2024-02/Caribbean%20sunset%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=EG_ct6K1 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="163" height="216"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Caribbean%20sunset%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=GIQmYtQn 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="144"/> <img width="327" height="144" src="/sites/default/files/styles/submenu_mobile/public/2024-02/Caribbean%20sunset%20-%20Hero.jpg.webp?itok=GIQmYtQn" alt="" loading="lazy" class="img-fluid" /> </picture><span class="submenu-text">Caribbean</span></div></a></div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></li><li class="menu-item nav-item"> <a href="https://oceanexpert.org/events/calendar?group=169" class="nav-link">Events</a><div class="normal menu_link_content menu-link-contentmain view-mode-level-0 dropdown-menu bg-primary"><div class="row submenu-wrapper"></div></div></li></ul></div> </nav><div id="block-unesco-unescosearchtextfield" class="block block-unesco-search block-unesco-search-textfield"><div data-block="sub_header"><form class="solr-header-search-form" data-drupal-selector="solr-header-search-form" action="/en/search" method="GET" id="solr-header-search-form" accept-charset="UTF-8"> <input data-drupal-selector="edit-category" type="hidden" name="category" value="Tsunami Programme of the International Oceanographic Commission" /><div data-drupal-selector="edit-wrapper-search-text" id="edit-wrapper-search-text" class="js-form-wrapper form-wrapper"><div class="js-form-item form-item js-form-type-textfield form-type-textfield js-form-item-query form-item-query form-no-label"> <label for="search-query" class="visually-hidden">Search</label> <input autocomplete="off" data-drupal-selector="search-query" type="text" id="search-query" name="query" value="" size="10" maxlength="255" placeholder="Search" class="form-text form-control" /></div><button class="btn btn-lg btn-primary custom-submit" label="ows-edit-submit" type="submit" data-drupal-selector="edit-button">Search</button></div></form></div></div></div></div> </header><main role="main" class="container"> <a id="main-content" tabindex="-1"></a><div class=""><div class="region region-content"><div class="unesco-search--dropdown block block-unesco-search block-unesco-search-solr" id="block-unesco-unescosearchsolr"><div class="unesco-search--overlay"></div><div class="btn unesco-search--close"></div><form class="solr-header-search-form" data-drupal-selector="solr-header-search-form-2" action="/en/search" method="GET" id="solr-header-search-form--2" accept-charset="UTF-8"> <input data-drupal-selector="edit-category" type="hidden" name="category" value="Tsunami Programme of the International Oceanographic Commission" /><div class="wrapper-search-text js-form-wrapper form-wrapper" data-drupal-selector="edit-wrapper-search-text" id="edit-wrapper-search-text--2"><div class="js-form-item form-item js-form-type-textfield form-type-textfield js-form-item-query form-item-query form-no-label"> <label for="search-query" class="visually-hidden">Search</label> <input autocomplete="off" data-drupal-selector="search-query" type="text" id="search-query" name="query" value="" size="64" maxlength="255" placeholder="Search" class="form-text form-control" /></div><button class="btn btn-lg btn-primary custom-submit" label="ows-edit-submit" type="submit" data-drupal-selector="edit-button">Search</button></div></form></div><div class="unesco-messages-wrapper"><div data-drupal-messages-fallback class="hidden"></div></div><div id="block-unesco-breadcrumbs" class="block block-system block-system-breadcrumb-block"> <nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><h2 id="system-breadcrumb" class="visually-hidden">Breadcrumb</h2><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"> <a href="/en/pacific">Pacific Ocean</a></li></ol> </nav></div><div id="block-unesco-content" class="block block-system block-system-main-block"> <article class="node--view-mode-full media-large node node--type-landing node--promoted" data-terms-tags="1823 1412 5539 4914 4855 2510 3233" data-terms-univers="1823" data-letter="I" data-nid="52"> <article data-terms-tags="1823 5531 5536 5539 4855 4914 5238 3233 2510" data-terms-univers="1823" data-letter="P" data-nid="48" class="node node--type-structured-data-hub node--promoted node--view-mode-header"><div class="node__content"><div class="header-hub" data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Header&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;html_element&quot;}}"><div class="hero-wrapper"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-banner"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_desktop/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=fmbpcRZn 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="1920" height="792"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_tablet/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=1oMhQOmn 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="800" height="406"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_mobile/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=74iyDu6U 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="400" height="512"/> <img loading="eager" width="400" height="512" fetchpriority="high" src="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_mobile/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=74iyDu6U" alt="Vast panoramic view of the Pacific Ocean into the horizon." title="Pacific Ocean" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div><div class="field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">Shutterstock. Jenna Aloia Photography</div></div></div><div class="header-texts"><div><a href="/en/pacific" class="title" hreflang="en">Pacific Ocean</a></div></div></div><div class="hub-menu-header hub-header-48"><ul class="menu menu-lvl1"><li class="menu-item"> <a href="/en/pacific" hreflang="en">Home</a></li><li class="menu-item"> <a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/pacific/icg-ptws" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/36">ICG/PTWS</a></li><li class="active menu-item"> <a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/pacific/itic" data-drupal-link-system-path="node/52" class="is-active" aria-current="page">ITIC</a></li></ul></div></div></div> </article><div class="node__content"><div class="header-landing" data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Header&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;html_element&quot;}}"><h1 class="title article-title">International Tsunami Information Centre</h1><div class="field field--name-field-description field--type-string-long field--label-hidden field__item">The International Tsunami Information Centre (ITIC) helps develop and provide info on tsunami warning systems, risks and good practices by engaging with Member States and the general public across the Pacific Ocean basin.</div></div><div ng-cloak="" ng-app="ods-widgets" class="field field--name-field-paragraphs field--type-entity-reference-revisions field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;International Tsunami Information Centre \u003E Paragraphs&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="" class="paragraph-border full paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-links field--type-link field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><a href="https://www.weather.gov/itic-car/tsunami_awareness_materials" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;For tsunami awareness materials&quot;}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">For tsunami awareness materials</a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://www.weather.gov/itic-car/itic_training" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;For ITIC tsunami training&quot;}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">For ITIC tsunami training</a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/tools-products/" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tools and Products&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;ced4065d-7e1a-4164-a23f-7915dfb80fa8&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Tools \u0026 Products&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Landing Page&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1757451653,&quot;modification&quot;:1761354060},&quot;tags&quot;:[]}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">Tools and Products</a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://www.weather.gov/itic-car/tsunami_event_lists" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tsunami Event Lists&quot;}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">Tsunami Event Lists</a></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Origins&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="origins" class="paragraph-border right paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Origins</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>The International Tsunami Information Centre (ITIC) was established through UNESCO-IOC Resolution IV-6 in November 1965 to support Member States of the ICG/PTWS.</p><p>Hosted by the US National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) National Weather Service in Honolulu, Hawaii, it operates from the Inouye Regional Center (IRC). The ITIC maintains and develops relationships with scientific research and academic organisations, civil defence agencies, and the general public in order to mitigate the hazards associated with tsunamis by improving tsunami preparedness for all Pacific Ocean nations.</p></div><div class="field field--name-field-links field--type-link field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><a href="/en/pacific/itic/map-directions-itic" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Map \u0026 Directions to ITIC&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;8d1a9981-6b83-4d15-84fa-6144e47729bd&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Map \u0026 Directions to ITIC&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Static Page&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1744238255,&quot;modification&quot;:1744243535},&quot;parent&quot;:{&quot;hub&quot;:&quot;Pacific Ocean&quot;},&quot;countries&quot;:[&quot;United States of America&quot;],&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;united states of america&quot;,&quot;asia and the pacific&quot;]}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">Map &amp; Directions to ITIC</a></div></div></div><div class="wrapper-image col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-medium"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-04/NOAA-IRC_rainbow_15Dec2017_N_Becker_cropped.jpg.webp?itok=a_gFHxj8 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="600" height="290"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_tablet/public/2025-04/NOAA-IRC_rainbow_15Dec2017_N_Becker_cropped.jpg.webp?itok=xNfUt3Mg 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="600" height="290"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_mobile/public/2025-04/NOAA-IRC_rainbow_15Dec2017_N_Becker_cropped.jpg.webp?itok=JEAu7Umt 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="158"/> <img loading="lazy" width="600" height="290" src="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-04/NOAA-IRC_rainbow_15Dec2017_N_Becker_cropped.jpg.webp?itok=a_gFHxj8" alt="NOAA Inouye Regional Center Building in Honolulu, Hawaii." title="NOAA Inouye Regional Center Building in Honolulu, Hawaii." class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div></div><div class="media--copyright field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">N. Becker</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Awareness materials&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;rich_text&quot;}}" id="awareness-materials" class="paragraph--hidden paragraph paragraph--type--rich-text paragraph--view-mode--default"></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Role of the ITIC&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="role-of-the-itic" class="paragraph-border left display-see-more paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Role of the ITIC</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>The ITIC's responsibilities include:</p><ul><li>Monitoring international tsunami warning activities in the Pacific and other oceans and recommending improvements in communications, data networks, acquisition and processing, tsunami forecasting methods, and information dissemination;</li><li>Bringing to Member and non-member States information on tsunami warning systems, on the affairs of UNESCO-IOC and ITIC, and on how to become active participants in the ICG/PTWS;</li><li>Assisting Member States in the establishment of national and regional warning systems, and the reduction of tsunami risk through comprehensive mitigation programmes;</li><li>Acting as a clearinghouse for the development of educational and preparedness materials, event data collection, and the fostering of research and its application to prevent loss of life.</li></ul></div></div><div class="wrapper-image col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-oembed-video media--view-mode-lightbox"> <a href="/en/unesco-media/206/lightbox" class="use-ajax" rel="nofollow" data-dialog-type="modal" data-dialog-options="{&quot;classes&quot;:{&quot;ui-dialog&quot;:&quot;resource-group-modal&quot;}}"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-visually_hidden"><div class="field__label visually-hidden">Thumbnail</div><div class="field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_full_desktop/public/oembed_thumbnails/LOT3Kx6zNNVtoXaFlQJjszyx17j7VVVGtplsoy5ryx8.jpg.webp?itok=dHN1P2_2 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="640" height="360"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_full_mobile/public/oembed_thumbnails/LOT3Kx6zNNVtoXaFlQJjszyx17j7VVVGtplsoy5ryx8.jpg.webp?itok=1DcPa1Uy 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="375" height="624"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_full_mobile/public/oembed_thumbnails/LOT3Kx6zNNVtoXaFlQJjszyx17j7VVVGtplsoy5ryx8.jpg.webp?itok=1DcPa1Uy 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="375" height="624"/> <img loading="lazy" width="375" height="624" src="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_full_mobile/public/oembed_thumbnails/LOT3Kx6zNNVtoXaFlQJjszyx17j7VVVGtplsoy5ryx8.jpg.webp?itok=1DcPa1Uy" alt="ITIC Informational Video" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div></div><div class="round round-lg"><i class="material-icons-sharp icon--video">play_arrow</i></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"VideoObject","@id":"https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/pacific/itic#video-206","name":"ITIC Informational Video","description":"ITIC Informational Video","thumbnailUrl":"https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/oembed_thumbnails/LOT3Kx6zNNVtoXaFlQJjszyx17j7VVVGtplsoy5ryx8.jpg","uploadDate":"2024-04-08T23:41:36+02:00","embedUrl":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/192771669","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/#organization","name":"IOC Tsunami Programme","url":"https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org"},"@reverse":{"video":{"@id":"https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/pacific/itic#webpage"}}}</script></a></div><div class="media--copyright field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">ITIC</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;International Tsunami Information Centre \u003E Paragraphs&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="" class="paragraph-border right paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Internationally, the <span>ITIC provides Impact-Based Decision Support Services (IDSS), outreach and training to countries participating to the Pacific Tsunami Warning and Mitigation System (PTWS) and the Tsunami and other Coastal Hazards Warning System for the Caribbean and Adjacent Regions (CARIBE-EWS), including the United States and the US Compact of Free Association countries of the Marshall Islands, Micronesia, and Palau. During tsunami events, ITIC provides remote real-time IDSS to countries as needed.</span></p><p>Domestically, the ITIC participates and supports the US National Tsunami Hazard Mitigation Program (NTHMP) that encompasses 28 coastal states, territories, and commonwealths, and includes NOAA, USGS and FEMA as the US Federal Agencies. ITIC especially supports the Pacific Tsunami Warning Center (PTWC) Area of Responsibility (Hawaii and Pacific-Caribbean insular states (American Samoa, Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands, Guam, Puerto Rico, US Virgin Islands) by providing Impact-Based Decision Support Services (IDSS), outreach and training. ITIC provides in-person IDSS to HI EMA during events.</p></div><div class="field field--name-field-links field--type-link field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/articles/noaa-daniel-k-inouye-regional-center-irc" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Read about ITIC\u0027s location at the NOAA IRC&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;8cb3a130-aa29-41cf-8f4b-28cdf80631f2&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;NOAA Daniel K. Inouye Regional Center (IRC)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Articles (local)&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1730972457,&quot;modification&quot;:1744238075},&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ocean&quot;,&quot;tsunami&quot;],&quot;subtype&quot;:&quot;article&quot;}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">Read about ITIC&#039;s location at the NOAA IRC</a></div></div></div><div class="wrapper-image col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-medium"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2024-11/ITIClibrary_DSC00422_crop_sml.jpg.webp?itok=yoI4RqDd 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="610" height="379"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_tablet/public/2024-11/ITIClibrary_DSC00422_crop_sml.jpg.webp?itok=hHyAOstp 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="700" height="435"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_mobile/public/2024-11/ITIClibrary_DSC00422_crop_sml.jpg.webp?itok=HDFSAy1M 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="203"/> <img loading="lazy" width="610" height="379" src="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2024-11/ITIClibrary_DSC00422_crop_sml.jpg.webp?itok=yoI4RqDd" alt="ITIC library" title="ITIC library" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div></div><div class="media--copyright field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">ITIC</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ITIC Caribbean Office&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="itic-caribbean-office" class="paragraph-border left paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>ITIC Caribbean Office</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p><span>The ITIC Caribbean Office (</span><a href="https://www.weather.gov/itic-car/"><span>ITIC-CAR</span></a><span>) was established in 2010 as the Caribbean Tsunami Warning Program, reorganized to the ITIC in 2017, and renamed in 2021.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>It monitors tsunami warning activities and facilitates tsunami preparedness in the US Territories of Puerto Rico and the US Virgin Islands and the wider Caribbean.&nbsp; The ITIC-CAR also provides support to the IOC's Caribbean Tsunami Information Centre and the Intergovernmental Coordination Group for the Tsunami and Other Coastal Hazards Warning System for the Caribbean and Adjacent Regions (</span><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/caribbean/icg-caribe-ews?hub=51"><span><u>ICG/CARIBE-EWS</u></span></a><span>).</span></p></div><div class="field field--name-field-links field--type-link field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><a href="/en/caribbean/ctic" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;More about CTIC&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;2b8144c0-1c8c-4075-a83a-243daaa696a4&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Caribbean Tsunami Information Centre&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Landing Page&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1712336032,&quot;modification&quot;:1741165961},&quot;parent&quot;:{&quot;hub&quot;:&quot;Caribbean&quot;},&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ocean&quot;,&quot;un \uff06 international cooperation&quot;,&quot;caribbean sea&quot;,&quot;tsunami&quot;,&quot;natural disasters&quot;]}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">More about CTIC</a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="/en/caribbean/icg-caribe-ews" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;More about ICG\/CARIBE-EWS&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;062fcca9-7911-4dfb-952d-e6f993914751&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Intergovernmental Coordination Group for the Tsunami and other Coastal Hazards Warning System for the Caribbean and Adjacent Regions (ICG\/CARIBE-EWS)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Landing Page&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1707405622,&quot;modification&quot;:1790939870},&quot;parent&quot;:{&quot;hub&quot;:&quot;Caribbean&quot;},&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ocean&quot;,&quot;social and human sciences&quot;,&quot;un \uff06 international cooperation&quot;]}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">More about ICG/CARIBE-EWS</a></div></div></div><div class="wrapper-image col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-medium"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-03/ITIC-CAR_Image.jpg.webp?itok=veCFzL_h 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="610" height="459"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_tablet/public/2025-03/ITIC-CAR_Image.jpg.webp?itok=pIoPlGcm 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="700" height="527"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_mobile/public/2025-03/ITIC-CAR_Image.jpg.webp?itok=IGWubVS4 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="246"/> <img loading="lazy" width="610" height="459" src="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-03/ITIC-CAR_Image.jpg.webp?itok=veCFzL_h" alt="ITIC-CAR" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div></div><div class="media--copyright field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">ITIC-CAR</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Contact&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;cards_landing&quot;}}" id="contact" class="paragraph paragraph--type--cards-landing paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Contact</h2></div><div class="row"><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-3"><div class="card card-height-fixed card-contact"><div class="card-body"><div class="field field--name-field-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/square_120/public/medias/image/people/2024/02/Laura%20Kong.jpeg.webp?itok=60r_H-jU" width="120" height="120" alt="Laura Kong" class="img-fluid image-style-square-120" /></div><div class="card-title">Laura Kong</div><p class="card-text">ITIC Director</p><p class="card-text"><p>NOAA</p><p>UNESCO-IOC</p></p></div><div class="card-footer"><div class="field field--name-field-email field--type-email field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="mailto:laura.kong@noaa.gov" target="_blank"><span class="round round-gray1"><i class="material-icons-sharp">mail</i></span><span class="visually-hidden">laura.kong@noaa.gov</span></a></div><div class="field field--name-field-social-networks field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="social-network"><a href="https://oceanexpert.org/expert/16046" target="_blank"><span class="round round-gray1"><i class="icon-oceanexpert icon"></i></span><span class="visually-hidden">Ocean Expert</span></a></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-3"><div class="card image-on-right card-height-fixed card-contact"><div class="card-body"><div class="card-circle"><i class="material-icons-sharp">people</i></div><div class="card-title">Nicol Alarcón Vergara</div><div class="card-text"><p>ITIC Associate Director</p><p><span>UNESCO-IOC</span></p><p>Head of Oceanographic Department</p><p>Hydrographic and Oceanographic Service of the Chilean Navy</p></div></div><div class="card-footer"><a href="mailto:nalarcon@shoa.cl" target="_blank"><span class="round round-white"><i class="material-icons-sharp">mail</i></span><span class="visually-hidden">nalarcon@shoa.cl</span></a></div></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-3"><div class="card card-height-fixed card-contact"><div class="card-body"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <img loading="lazy" src="/sites/default/files/styles/square_120/public/2024-08/Christa_Photo.png.webp?itok=AcFrcN4J" width="120" height="120" alt="Christa" class="img-fluid image-style-square-120" /></div><div class="card-title">Christa von Hillebrandt-Andrade</div><p class="card-text"><p>ITIC Deputy Director</p><p>ITIC CAR Manager</p><p>NOAA</p><p>UNESCO-IOC</p></p></div><div class="card-footer"><div class="field field--name-field-email field--type-email field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="mailto:christa.vonh@noaa.gov" target="_blank"><span class="round round-gray1"><i class="material-icons-sharp">mail</i></span><span class="visually-hidden">christa.vonh@noaa.gov</span></a></div><div class="field field--name-field-social-networks field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="social-network"><a href="https://oceanexpert.org/expert/16872" target="_blank"><span class="round round-gray1"><i class="icon-oceanexpert icon"></i></span><span class="visually-hidden">Ocean Expert</span></a></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-3"><div class="card card-height-fixed card-contact"><div class="card-body"><div class="card-circle bg-blueLight"><i class="material-icons-sharp">people</i></div><div class="card-title">Tammy Fukuji</div><p class="card-text">ITIC Information Technology Specialist</p><p class="card-text"><p>NOAA</p><p>UNESCO-IOC</p></p></div><div class="card-footer"><div class="field field--name-field-email field--type-email field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="mailto:tammy.fukuji@noaa.gov" target="_blank"><span class="round round-gray1"><i class="material-icons-sharp">mail</i></span><span class="visually-hidden">tammy.fukuji@noaa.gov</span></a></div><div class="field field--name-field-social-networks field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><div class="social-network"><a href="https://oceanexpert.org/expert/20140" target="_blank"><span class="round round-gray1"><i class="icon-oceanexpert icon"></i></span><span class="visually-hidden">Ocean Expert</span></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Programmes \u0026 activities&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;faq&quot;}}" id="programmes--activities" class="paragraph-border paragraph paragraph--type--faq paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Programmes &amp; activities</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>As part of its international mandate to foster and disseminate information on tsunami awareness, forecasting, and mitigation, the ITIC's programmes cover a wide range of activities and services.</p></div><div class="bg-gray1 accordion accordion-flush rounded field field--name-field-ref-faqs field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-127" aria-expanded="false">Tsunami Education, Preparedness, Training</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-127"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p>Both tsunami risk reduction and effective tsunami warning systems require a comprehensive approach consisting of warning guidance, risk assessment, and preparedness and education.</p><p>The ITIC’s mitigation programme is directed towards coastal residents, their national and local officials, school teachers, mass media, policy makers, and the general public. Through training classes, lectures, community briefings, and media broadcasts, it ensures a prepared and aware public can always know how to respond to tsunami emergencies to reduce tsunami impacts and save lives.</p><p>The ITIC's <a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/training#pacific-ocean">ITP-Hawaii Programme</a> on tsunami warning and mitigation systems allows scientists, engineers, and tsunami programme officials to spend up to three weeks in Hawaii learning about tsunamis, warning system operation, risk assessment, and education and preparedness programmes alongside experts and local civil defence agencies.</p><p>The ITIC also conducts the ITP-International Programme, which annually visits Member States to provide in-country capacity assessments, and tsunami awareness and technology training.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-128" aria-expanded="false">Tsunami Research</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-128"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">For each tsunami, the ITIC assists the <a href="https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/hazard/tsu.shtml">World Data Service World Data System for Geophysics, co-located at the NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information</a>, in soliciting and collecting seismic information and tsunami wave records, together with supplementary data and descriptive information on tsunami damage.</p><p class="text-align-justify">This allows the ITIC to:</p><ul><li><p class="text-align-justify">Prepare and disseminate a report on the tsunami through its quarterly Tsunami Newsletter;</p></li><li><p class="text-align-justify">Maintain an extensive data file and comprehensive library available to researchers, government officials, and the general public;</p></li><li><p class="text-align-justify">Identify research needed to improve tsunami prediction and the International Warning System;</p></li><li><p class="text-align-justify">Cooperate with national, international, and professional organisations in encouraging and applying tsunami research;</p></li><li><p class="text-align-justify">Facilitate and coordinate International Tsunami Survey Teams to conduct&nbsp;field investigations of destructive large tsunamis, following the procedures and guidance provided in the IOC Post-Tsunami Survey Field Guide (IOC TS 37, 2d ed, 2014).</p></li></ul></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-129" aria-expanded="false">Tsunami Technology and Information</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-129"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">The ITIC provides tsunami data and information to scientists, engineers, administrators, and the general public throughout the world.</p><ul><li><p class="text-align-justify">It enables access to technical information that renders tsunami warning systems more effective, and ensures knowledge of new technology and mitigation countermeasures is available to all Member States.</p></li><li><p class="text-align-justify">It also provides advisory and consulting services to Member States, wishing to initiate or upgrade their warning and mitigation system capability, and also works closely with ICGs and their Working Groups to identify and recommend programme enhancements to regional tsunami warning systems and Member States' national systems.</p></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Public Relations and Publications&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;rich_text&quot;}}" id="public-relations-and-publications" class="paragraph paragraph--type--rich-text paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Public Relations and Publications</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p><strong>Public Relations</strong></p><p>The ITIC maintains working relationships with national and international organizations participating in the International Tsunami Warning System. Public relations are maintained with the media with the goal of achieving an informed public.</p><p><strong>Publications</strong></p><p><span>The ITIC prepares and publishes tsunami research reports and papers, historical tsunami catalogs, glossaries, bibliographies, books, and educational materials. It maintains a web site through the IOC with information on the International Tsunami Warning System with FAQs on tsunamis and tsunami preparedness. It publishes the Tsunami Newsletter that brings to researchers, engineers, educators, and government officials a summary of the year's tsunamis and other activities related to the Tsunami Warning System. It is distributed to approximately forty countries and is available electronically and in hard copy.</span></p></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ITIC Working with ICG\/PTWS&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="itic-working-with-icg-ptws" class="paragraph-border left paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>ITIC Working with ICG/PTWS</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Under the auspices of the Intergovernmental Oceanographic Commission (IOC), the&nbsp;Intergovernmental Coordination Group for the Pacific Tsunami Warning&nbsp;and Mitigation System&nbsp;first convened in 1968 (ICG/PTWS, formerly known as ICG/ITSU for International Tsunami). At that time, the IOC established the International Tsunami Information Centre (ITIC), which is currently staffed by the U.S.A and Chile. The ITIC supports the work plan of the ICG/PTWS, and works directly with Member States to strengthen their national tsunami warning and mitigation systems.&nbsp;</p><p><span>The ITIC works closely with the IOC Tsunami Service Providers (TSP, NOAA’s Richard H. Hagemeyer&nbsp;</span><u>Pacific Tsunami Warning Center&nbsp;(PTWC)</u><span>, Japan's</span><u> Northwest Pacific Tsunami Advisory Center (NWPTAC)</u><span>, China's </span><u>South China Sea Tsunami Advisory Centre</u><span>, Nicaragua's <u>Central America Tsunami Advisory Centre (CATAC, interim service since 2022)</u>&nbsp;to ensure that Member States understand how to use the tsunami threat advice to guide their national tsunami warning decision-making. &nbsp;The ITIC also works with the </span><u>US National Tsunami Warning Center (US NTWC)</u><span>, which provides warning services for Canada through bi-lateral arrangements.</span></p></div></div><div class="wrapper-image col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-medium"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image%201.jpg.webp?itok=KEXCG74B 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="468" height="288"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_tablet/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image%201.jpg.webp?itok=rrIrx-B5 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="468" height="288"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_mobile/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image%201.jpg.webp?itok=zL7q9Nd8 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="201"/> <img loading="lazy" width="468" height="288" src="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image%201.jpg.webp?itok=KEXCG74B" alt="Coastal areas of responsibility of PTWC, US NTWC, and NWPTAC in the PTWS" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div></div><div class="media--copyright field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">ITIC</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;International Tsunami Information Centre \u003E Paragraphs&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;text_media_block&quot;}}" id="" class="paragraph-border left paragraph paragraph--type--text-media-block paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="row"><div class="wrapper-infos col-lg-6"><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p><strong>The following countries/territories have official PTWS Tsunami National Contact and Tsunami Warning Focal Point designations,&nbsp;and receive IOC tsunami information:</strong></p><p>Australia,&nbsp;Brunei Darussalam, Canada, Chile, China, China Hong Kong, Colombia, Cook Islands, Costa Rica, Ecuador, El Salvador, Fiji, France, Guatemala, Honduras, Japan, Kiribati, Malaysia, Mexico, Nauru, New Zealand, Nicaragua, Palau, Panama, Peru, Philippines, Samoa, Singapore, Solomon Islands, Thailand, Tonga, Tuvalu, United States, Vanuatu, Vietnam</p><p><strong>The following countries/territories do not have officially-designated PTWS Tsunami National Contact and/or Tsunami Warning Focal Point designations, but do receive IOC tsunami information:</strong></p><p>Cambodia, Democratoc Republic of Timor-Lester (East Timor),&nbsp;Federated States of Micronesia (Chuuk, Kosrae, Pohnpei, Yap), France (French Polynesia, New Caledonia, Wallis &amp; Futuna), Indonesia, Republic of Marshall Islands (Kwajalein, Majuro), Niue, Papua New Guinea, Republic of Korea (South Korea), Russian Federation, Tokelau, United Kingdom (National, Pitcairn Islands), United States (Midway, Wake)</p><p><strong>The following countries/territories do not have officially-designated PTWS Tsunami National Contact and Tsunami Warning Focal Point designations, and do not receive IOC tsunami information:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Democratic Republic of Korea (North Korea)</p><p>Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, Federated States of Micronesia, Republic of Marshall Islands, Nauru, and Tokelau are not Member States of the IOC, but are Member States of UNESCO.</p></div></div><div class="wrapper-image col-lg-6"><div class="field field--name-field-ref-image field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-medium"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image_2.jpg.webp?itok=Fm7z97HD 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="610" height="321"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_tablet/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image_2.jpg.webp?itok=bogOBLnW 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="700" height="369"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_mobile/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image_2.jpg.webp?itok=UobOKFOH 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="327" height="172"/> <img loading="lazy" width="610" height="321" src="/sites/default/files/styles/paragraph_medium_desktop/public/2025-05/ITIC%20Working%20with%20ICG%20PTWS_Image_2.jpg.webp?itok=Fm7z97HD" alt="Area of Services (AoS)" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div></div><div class="media--copyright field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">ITIC</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Working with others&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;faq&quot;}}" id="working-with-others" class="paragraph-border paragraph paragraph--type--faq paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Working with others</h2></div><div class="rich-text clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p><span>As an international centre with focus on tsunamis, the ITIC has for many years worked with organisations around the world to heighten awareness in order to encourage the building of better technical warning systems, and a better prepared public.</span></p><p><span>Towards these ends, the ITIC and IOC&nbsp;maintains and develops relationships with:</span></p></div><div class="bg-gray1 accordion accordion-flush rounded field field--name-field-ref-faqs field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-180" aria-expanded="false">Intergovernmental and United Nations Organisations</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-180"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">All Member States of UNESCO, IOC and its Intergovernmental Coordination Groups for Tsunami Warning and Mitigation; International Union of Geodesy and Geophysics (IUGG); World Data Service and System Centers (WDS); World Meteorological Organization (WMO); International Hydrographic Organizaton (IHO); UN Office for Disaster Risk Reduction (UNISDR); UN Development Program (UNDP); UN&nbsp;<span> Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UNESCAP); </span>International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC); International Telecommunications Union (ITU), and other &nbsp;development, environmental, and technical aganecies in disaster risk reduction.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-181" aria-expanded="false">Regional Organisations</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-181"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">Regional science, technical, meteorological, and disaster management organizations include the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN),&nbsp;Asian Disaster Reduction Center (ADRC), Asia Disaster Preparedness Center (ADPC), South Pacific Community (formerly SOPAC), Secretariat of the Pacific Regional Environment Programme (SPREP), Centro de Coordinación para la Prevención de los Desastres Naturales en América Central (CEPREDENAC), Permanent Commission for the South Pacific (CPPS), and Caribbean Disaster Emergency Management Agency (CDEMA).</p></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-182" aria-expanded="false">Scientific Community</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-182"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">Scientists and researchers in academic organisations, universities, and institutions worldwide. Gaining a better understanding through research of how tsunamis are generated, propagate , and inundate our coasts is critical for savings lives and reducing impacts to property and infrastructure. &nbsp;Post-tsunami science and social science surveys after destructive events collect the data needs to improve our predictions and forecasts, and build stronger, tsunami-resistant structures.</p><p>International science organisations which collect and archive data include</p><ul><li>WDC-SEG-TSUNAMIS / NGDC – for the collection and archiving of significant tsunami events and building of a global, high-quality, referenced database, including both run-ups, wave and earthquake observations, and also sea level mareograms. &nbsp;WDC-SEG-TSUNAMIS / NGDC – for the collection and archiving of significant tsunami events and building of a global, high-quality, referenced database, including both run-ups, wave and earthquake observations, and also sea level mareograms. &nbsp;</li><li>IUGG-Tsunami Commission – for the encouragement of tsunami research, organization of post-tsunami international tsunami surveys to collect perishable data to improve hydrodynamic models and develop tsunami-resistant engineering guidelines, co-sponsorship of tsunami workshops to highlight issue of common priority and also to bring tsunami science to countries through pre-ICG/PTWS workshops. &nbsp;ITIC and NGDC work together with IUGG-TC.</li><li>US Geological Survey &nbsp;/ IRIS Global Seismic Network (GSN) / Federation of Digital Broadband Seismographic Networks (FDSN) – for the cooperation to install and support real-time continuous waveform data streams that are essential for tsunami warning monitoring. &nbsp;Installation of high-quality, broadband stations (STS-1, or STS-2 or equivalent), and free and open data sharing are essential for issuing timely warnings since seismic waves travel more than 40 times faster than tsunami waves. &nbsp;The USGS provides both earthquake monitoring on 7x24 basis, and also provides infrastructure through which the GSN data is made available. &nbsp;The FDSN is the overarching international coordination organisation to which the ITIC hopes every country contributing to seismic monitoring will join.</li><li>University of Hawaii Sea Level Center (UHSLC) / IOC Global Sea Level Observing System Group of Experts Chair (GLOSS GE) – as a resource supporting and installing sea level stations in the IOTWS since 2005, for the continued e forts over that last decades with the Pacific through numerous programmes, and as a resource for IOTWS and PTWS Sea Level Working Groups for data collection platforms and station configurations, transmission arrangements and standards, and data archiving of GLOSS stations.</li></ul></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-183" aria-expanded="false">Countries and Local Officials</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-183"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">The ITIC informs Member States of developments in tsunami research and education, and develops and distributes awareness materials globally. The ITIC initiates, co-ordinates, and/or conducts technical training programmes, workshops, and seminars dealing with all aspects of tsunami preparedeness to help countries strengthen their national tsunami warning and mitigation systems. The ITIC aims to make authorities more aware of the tsunami hazard, and assists in planning programs for the protection of life and property and for evacuations from dangerous areas during tsunami warnings.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item accordion-item"><div class="faq"><h3 class="faq-title accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed fw-bold" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-184" aria-expanded="false">General Public</button></h3><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="collapse-184"><div class="faq-text accordion-body"><p class="text-align-justify">The ITIC informs the general public of the tsunami hazard through lectures, publications, educational materials and disaster preparedness programs, and participates in local outreach and preparedness fairs and training. The ITIC provides information on the latest tsunami alerts issued by the PTWC, NWPTAC, US NTWC, and other IOC Tsunami Service Providers.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tsunami Exercises&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;cards_landing&quot;}}" id="tsunami-exercises" class="paragraph paragraph--type--cards-landing paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Tsunami Exercises</h2></div><div class="row"><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-3"> <a class="card card-height-fixed card-text card-overlay card-link-wrapper" data-uri-image-style="/sites/default/files/styles/card_1_column/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=hv3pBohm" data-uri-image-style-mobile="/sites/default/files/styles/card_1_column/public/2024-02/Pacific%20Ocean.jpg.webp?itok=hv3pBohm" href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/pacwave" title="Pacific Exercise" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Pacific Exercise&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;3316e66f-99fa-4932-88fa-9ffb964bb88a&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;PACWAVE &quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Static Page&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1724915259,&quot;modification&quot;:1792785332},&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ocean&quot;,&quot;programme implementation&quot;,&quot;tsunami&quot;,&quot;pacific ocean&quot;],&quot;video&quot;:{&quot;exists&quot;:true}}}"><div class="card-arrow arrow-black"></div><div class="card-body"><div class="card-title">Pacific Exercise</div><div class="card-text"><p>Please find the PacWave!</p></div></div> </a></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-3"> <a class="card card-height-fixed card-text card-overlay card-link-wrapper" data-uri-image-style="/sites/default/files/styles/card_1_column/public/2025-09/shutterstock_2499399123.jpg.webp?itok=OvhOutZK" data-uri-image-style-mobile="/sites/default/files/styles/card_1_column/public/2025-09/shutterstock_2499399123.jpg.webp?itok=OvhOutZK" href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/en/exercises" title="International Exercises" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;International Exercises&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;8c953fba-f38b-4b49-b325-95d156761297&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Wave Exercises&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Landing Page&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;publication&quot;:1705984628,&quot;modification&quot;:1751509100},&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;ocean&quot;,&quot;programme implementation&quot;,&quot;sharing knowledge&quot;,&quot;un \uff06 international cooperation&quot;,&quot;tsunami&quot;],&quot;unesdoc_refs&quot;:[&quot;0000218967&quot;]}}"><div class="card-arrow arrow-black"></div><div class="card-body"><div class="card-title">International Exercises</div><div class="card-text"><p>Please click to look at the exercises in different regions!</p></div></div> </a></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Contact ITIC&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;banner_cta&quot;}}" id="contact-itic" class="paragraph-simple position-full paragraph paragraph--type--banner-cta paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="media media--type-image media--view-mode-banner"><div class="field field--name-field-media-image field--type-image field--label-hidden field__item"> <picture> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_desktop/public/2024-11/IMG_1318_web_0.jpg.webp?itok=7A-oKfex 1x" media="all and (min-width: 993px)" type="image/webp" width="1920" height="792"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_tablet/public/2024-11/IMG_1318_web_0.jpg.webp?itok=H0SbrBNd 1x" media="all and (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 992px)" type="image/webp" width="800" height="406"/> <source srcset="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_mobile/public/2024-11/IMG_1318_web_0.jpg.webp?itok=Y1CcmTog 1x" media="all and (max-width: 575px)" type="image/webp" width="400" height="512"/> <img loading="eager" width="400" height="512" fetchpriority="high" src="/sites/default/files/styles/banner_mobile/public/2024-11/IMG_1318_web_0.jpg.webp?itok=Y1CcmTog" alt="NOAA Daniel K. Inouye Regional Center (IRC)" title="NOAA Daniel K. Inouye Regional Center (IRC)" class="img-fluid" /> </picture></div><div class="field field--name-field-copyright field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item">ITIC</div></div><div class="banner-cta-texts border"><h3 class="paragraph-title banner-cta-title">Contact ITIC</h3><p class="banner-cta-description">The International Tsunami Information Center is located at the NOAA Daniel K. Inouye Regional Center (IRC). Address is 1845 Wasp Boulevard, Building 176, Honolulu, HI 96818 USA. Contact us by phone at +1 808 725 6050 or by fax at +1 808 725 6055.</p><div class="field field--name-field-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item"><a href="mailto:itic.tsunami@noaa.gov" data-trk="{&quot;cta&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Email ITIC&quot;}}" class="btn btn-primary btn-arrow-right">Email ITIC</a></div></div></div></div><div class="field__item"><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Resolutions&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;quick_link&quot;}}" id="resolutions" class="paragraph-border -two-column paragraph paragraph--type--quick-link paragraph--view-mode--default"><div class="field field--name-field-title field--type-string field--label-hidden field__item"><h2>Resolutions</h2></div><div class="field field--name-field-description field--type-string-long field--label-hidden field__item">Read the IOC resolutions across five decades that have shaped the history of ITIC and its mission to save lives from tsunami risk.</div><div class="field field--name-field-links field--type-link field--label-hidden field__items"><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2024/11/1965_ioc4_res6.pdf"><div class="link-wrapper"><span class="arrow-primary"></span><span class="link-title">Establishment of ITSU and ITIC (Resolution IV-6, 1965)</span></div></a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2024/11/clno748_resec-iv.6.pdf"><div class="link-wrapper"><span class="arrow-primary"></span><span class="link-title">Establishment of ITIC Associate Director (Resolution EC-IV.6, 1974)</span></div></a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2024/11/1977_ioc10_res23.pdf"><div class="link-wrapper"><span class="arrow-primary"></span><span class="link-title">Mandate and functions for the Pacific (Resolution X-23, 1977)</span></div></a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2024/11/1988_ec21_res4.pdf"><div class="link-wrapper"><span class="arrow-primary"></span><span class="link-title">Amendment to mandate (Resolution EC-XXI.4, 1988)</span></div></a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2024/11/2005_iocxxiii_res12-14_145407e.pdf"><div class="link-wrapper"><span class="arrow-primary"></span><span class="link-title">Request to support global system development (Resolution XXIII-12, 13, 14, 2005)</span></div></a></div><div class="field__item"><a href="https://tsunami.ioc.unesco.org/sites/default/files/medias/fichiers/2024/11/2006_ioc-ecxxxix_res8.pdf"><div class="link-wrapper"><span class="arrow-primary"></span><span class="link-title">Renaming of ITSU to PTWS with ITIC as interim PTWS Secretariat (Resolution EC-X…</span></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;end-content&quot;}}" class="data-trk-end-content"></div><div data-trk="{&quot;block&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Related items&quot;}}" class="content-tags"><div class="item-list"><h3>Related items</h3><ul><li><a href="/en/tags/ocean" class="tag tag-outline-grey" hreflang="en">Ocean</a></li><li><a href="/en/tags/social-and-human-sciences" class="tag tag-outline-grey" hreflang="en">Social and human sciences</a></li><li><a href="/en/tags/un-international-cooperation" class="tag tag-outline-grey" 